## Email Generation

### Campaign Arc (5-Email Sequence)

| Email | Send Day | Theme | Goal |
|-------|----------|-------|------|
| 1 | Day 0 | Revenue Visibility Problem | Hook with persona pain point. Introduce Wayroo. Soft CTA. |
| 2 | Day 3 | Customer Story | Social proof — similar company, similar role, real outcome. |
| 3 | Day 7 | POS Feature Spotlight | One specific feature relevant to their industry. Include a stat or data point. |
| 4 | Day 12 | ROI Framing | Simple math: faster close rates, better forecast accuracy. |
| 5 | Day 17 | Meeting Request | Direct, warm ask. Calendly link prominent. Soft urgency. |

### Personalization Rules

Always personalize to the lead's:
- **First name** — use it in the greeting
- **Company name** — reference it naturally in the body
- **Industry** — tailor the pain point and feature reference to their vertical
- **Title tier** — VPs get peer-level framing ("as a revenue leader…"); Directors get aspirational framing ("as you scale your team…")

### Industry-Specific Pain Points (use in Email 1 & 3)

- **Restaurant/Food Service:** "your CRM shows a healthy pipeline, but POS data tells a different story at each location"
- **Grocery:** "forecasting feels like guesswork when POS and CRM don't talk to each other"
- **Hospitality:** "revenue leaks hiding in POS data that never makes it to the sales team"
- **Specialty Retail:** "tying rep activity to actual sell-through at each location"

### Email Format

```
Subject: [under 50 characters, persona-resonant, no spam words]

Hi [First Name] —

[1-2 sentence hook: industry-specific pain point]

[1-2 sentences: how Wayroo solves it, referencing POS specifically]

[1 sentence: social proof or outcome reference — optional in Email 1]

[CTA: single, clear ask — book a time or reply]

[Calendly link or reply prompt]
```

